            <ArticleTitle>Imaging features of bariatric surgery and its complications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>311-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.sult.2013.04.005</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0887-2171(13)00046-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnostic imaging features of the most commonly performed types of bariatric surgery, which are gastric banding, sleeve gastrectomy, and Roux-en-Y gastric bypass, are reviewed as well as imaging diagnosis of their complications. Although upper gastrointestinal series remains the first-line imaging test for assessing postoperative anatomy and complications, the important role of multidetector computed tomography in diagnosis of serious complications is highlighted.</AbstractText>
